-- title:
--   Boolean validation of sharp band data
-- statement:
--   Let $d$ be band data, let $t_0,t_1,c,q$ be stored rationals, and let $E$ be the
--   stored argument enclosure. Suppose the heights, center $1/2+i\operatorname{val}(c)$,
--   and radius $\sqrt{\operatorname{val}(q)}$ of $d$ agree with those data. Then
--   $$\operatorname{validBS}(t_0,t_1,c,q,d.n,E)=\mathrm{true}
--   \quad\Longrightarrow\quad
--   \operatorname{ValidS}\!\left(\tfrac1{4000000},\tfrac{3999999}{4000000},
--   \operatorname{withEncl}(d,E)\right).$$
--   This turns the finite rational checker into the analytic side conditions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/DrMurphyIsIn/Arda/blob/af4fde8972eb6d4e78c7d9a95933b18b81adf52d/telperion/examples/zeta_reflection/lean/H11K_Turing.lean#L235-L263

